      "markdown": "## Cramer's Rule for Linear Systems of Three Equations\n\n $$ a_{11}x_{1}+a_{12}x_{2}+a_{13}x_{3}=b_{1} $$ \n\n $$ a_{21}x_{1}+a_{22}x_{2}+a_{23}x_{3}=b_{2} $$ \n\n $$ a_{31}x_{1}+a_{32}x_{2}+a_{33}x_{3}=b_{3} $$ \n\nis\n\n $$ x_{1}=\\frac{D_{1}}{D},\\quad x_{2}=\\frac{D_{2}}{D},\\quad x_{3}=\\frac{D_{3}}{D} $$ \n\nwith the determinant D of the system given by (4) and\n\n $$ D_{1}=\\left|\\begin{matrix}b_{1}&a_{12}&a_{13}\\\\ b_{2}&a_{22}&a_{23}\\\\ b_{3}&a_{32}&a_{33}\\\\ \\end{matrix}\\right|,\\quad D_{2}=\\left|\\begin{matrix}a_{11}&b_{1}&a_{13}\\\\ a_{21}&b_{2}&a_{23}\\\\ a_{31}&b_{3}&a_{33}\\\\ \\end{matrix}\\right|,\\quad D_{3}=\\left|\\begin{matrix}a_{11}&a_{12}&b_{1}\\\\ a_{21}&a_{22}&b_{2}\\\\ a_{31}&a_{32}&b_{3}\\\\ \\end{matrix}\\right|. $$ \n\nNote that $D_{1}, D_{2}, D_{3}$ are obtained by replacing Columns 1, 2, 3, respectively, by the column of the right sides of (5).",
